The `cookedprint` function contains a potential buffer overrun vulnerability. Specifically, the lines:

```c
	atoascii(name, MAXVARLEN, bn, sizeof(bn));
	if (output_raw != '*') {
		atoascii(value, MAXVALLEN,
			 bv, sizeof(bv) - 1);
		len = strlen(bv);
		bv[len] = output_raw;
		bv[len+1] = '\0';
	} else {
